{
  "title": "Guitar hanger: a wall mount that cradles a Telecaster's neck",
  "description": "A wall hanger for a six-string Telecaster, hung by its neck: the neck sits in a U just below the headstock, which rests on the U's two arms. Printed lying on its back (the wall side on the bed), so z is out from the wall, y up the wall. Only the two screw bosses on the wall and the two arm pads the headstock rests on are kept; the optimiser grows the arms from the bosses to the pads, braced against the guitar's weight (4 kg, with a margin), a tug away from the wall and a knock sideways. The gap between the arms clears the neck at the nut (42 mm) with room for a foam pad each side, and is narrower than the headstock. 12% of a 110 × 130 × 70 mm space on 2.5 mm cells, struts at least 6.5 mm, printable without supports in the +z direction.",
  "uses": [
    "x1c"
  ],
  "material": "pla",
